Source: lazyjira
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Dario Griffo <dariogriffo@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/textfuel/lazyjira
Package: lazyjira
Version: lazyjira_VERSION-BUILD_VERSION~DIST
Architecture: SUPPORTED_ARCHITECTURES
Suggests: git, xclip, xdg-utils
Description: terminal UI for Jira, in the style of lazygit
 lazyjira is a fast, keyboard-driven terminal user interface for Jira Cloud
 and Jira Server/Data Center, modelled on lazygit. A four-panel layout shows
 issues, projects, the selected issue and its status side by side, with
 vim-style navigation and mouse support.
 .
 It offers JQL search with autocomplete, highlighting and history, and inline
 editing of transitions, priority, assignee, labels, comments and descriptions
 (in $EDITOR), as well as issue creation. Keybindings, JQL tabs, issue columns,
 custom fields and colour themes are configurable. The first run starts a
 setup wizard for the Jira connection.
 .
 The optional helpers are only suggested: git enables creating and checking
 out branches named after issues, xclip enables copying to the clipboard and
 xdg-utils enables opening issues in the web browser.
